# LocalBook — Cursor Context

## Project summary
Full-stack appointment booking app for local SMBs. React + Firebase.
No backend server — everything runs client-side + Firestore.

## Stack
- React 18 + Vite (ESM)
- Tailwind CSS
- Firebase 10 (Auth + Firestore + Hosting)
- react-router-dom v6

## File structure
```
localbook/
  src/
    App.jsx              ← routing
    firebase.js          ← Firebase init
    index.css            ← Tailwind imports
    main.jsx             ← React entry
    hooks/
      useAuth.js         ← onAuthStateChanged wrapper
    pages/
      Landing.jsx        ← homepage + Sign-In
      Dashboard.jsx      ← owner tabs
      BookingPage.jsx    ← 4-step public booking flow
    components/
      BusinessSetup.jsx
      ServicesManager.jsx
      HoursManager.jsx
      BlockedDates.jsx
      BookingsCalendar.jsx
    utils/
      slots.js           ← generateTimeSlots, formatTime, getDayName
  firestore.rules
  firebase.json
  .env.example
```

## Routes
| Path | Component | Auth required |
|------|-----------|--------------|
| / | Landing | No |
| /dashboard | Dashboard | Yes (Google) |
| /book/:businessId | BookingPage | No |

## Coding conventions
- React functional components only
- useState + useEffect for local state
- All Firestore reads/writes in the component that needs them
- Tailwind only — no CSS modules, no styled-components
- Keep slot generation in utils/slots.js
- Confirm destructive actions with window.confirm()

